  "verbalization": "Fucatoside B appears to interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through a shared target, HL-60, which is targeted by multiple compounds, including (-)-Licarin B, Centaurein, and Sagittasine C. This suggests that Fucatoside B may exert its effects via a mechanism that involves the HL-60 cell line, potentially through a common pathway or a distinct but related mechanism. The evidence indicates that Fucatoside B could act as a modulator of Phosphodiesterase 6C, possibly by influencing the activity of HL-60 cells, which are known to be sensitive to various compounds. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting HL-60 implies that Fucatoside B might be part of a broader network of interactions that influence cellular processes through this shared target.",
